From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:00:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban start gate: skip record, expected hold,
 pickup, fail open on discovery faults

Review of 73aeb3f0: a gated card left no record, so pickup re-imported it
every tick, the dispatcher-stuck detector counted it as unexplained and
diagnostics called it stranded; and a plugin-discovery fault outside the
caught classes could escape into the tick.

A gated start now records a dispatch_skipped skip (reason start_gate), is an
expected hold for the stuck detector, is named by held_in_ready diagnostics,
and is skipped at pickup like a governor hold. The gate catches every fault
and warns once per process. Still not a respawn-guard hold: no cap, no
auto-block, nothing counted against the card.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
